Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:05.850
An extended Disney princess scene, cameos
by Kylo Ren and the Golden Girls, plus more

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:09.820
Fix-It Felix and Calhoun are just some of
the many scenes cut from Ralph Breaks The

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:10.820
Internet.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:14.580
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and today I'm revealing everything that was

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:19.050
deleted from the Wreck-It Ralph sequel including
some incredible cameos and jokes you may wish

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:20.570
had been in the movie!

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:25.020
Keep watching to the end to find out the amazing
extended Stan Lee scene that didn't make it

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.510
in to the final film.

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:31.300
My Funko Pops giveaway is also running on
this video, so hit the bell and tap the Gleam

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.520
link in the video description to enter.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.200
Mild spoilers ahead, though I've kept them
to a minimum, and there are no spoilers for

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.540
the ending.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:42.800
The Disney princess team-up in Ralph Breaks
The Internet is one of the movie's highlights,

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.500
however, originally the scene played out rather
differently.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:50.729
In early versions of the story, Vanellope,
Ralph and Yesss were all at OhMyDisney together

00:00:50.729 --> 00:00:53.229
and saw the princesses greeting fans there.

00:00:53.229 --> 00:00:58.020
Yesss gave Vanellope a tour of the Disney
fan site and Stormtroopers escorted the princesses

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:00.549
backstage where Vanellope followed them.

00:01:00.549 --> 00:01:06.260
Footage shown at Disney's D23 Expo in 2017
also revealed several extra jokes cut from

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:07.440
the final film.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:12.030
For example, Jasmine was allergic to cats
and her pet tiger Rajah looked at her slightly

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.320
offended as she puffed on an inhaler.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:19.230
And Snow White always looked surprised because
she was secretly "legally blind" and needed

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:21.310
a pair of thick glasses.

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:25.610
C-3PO also originally had an extended scene
with the princesses after he arrived in the

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:28.680
green room to tell them there was another
"Which Disney princess are you?"

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:30.240
quiz about to start.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:35.520
In the deleted footage, Cinderella replied,
"why thank you R2-D2" and the other princesses

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:37.540
joined in poking fun at him.

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:41.610
Sleeping Beauty told Cinderella that the Star
Wars droid "hates [being] called that", but

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:44.060
then trolled him with the line "we'll be right
there, BB-8!"

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:49.150
C-3PO, feeling mortally offended, walked out
mumbling, "Such insolence.

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:51.520
'You're good with princesses,' they said.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:52.710
'You'll love this job.'

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:56.050
… Oh, how I long for the days of Captain
Solo."

00:01:56.050 --> 00:02:00.570
These extended jokes were probably deleted
to create better comedy timing in the scene

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:05.560
and better pacing in the movie overall, but
I wonder whether the C-3PO jokes ended up

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:09.750
being trimmed because some Star Wars fans
were disappointed that their iconic Princess

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:11.660
Leia didn't appear in the scene.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:16.841
The Wreck-It Ralph 2 filmmakers decided to
only use so-called "canonized" Disney Princesses

00:02:16.841 --> 00:02:21.560
from the "official" Disney line for the scene,
excluding various other princesses from Disney

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:25.210
animated movies and Disney-owned properties
like Star Wars.

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:29.920
They did, however, add Elsa, Anna and Moana
who aren't part of the official princess line-up,

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:34.310
but they are hugely popular and it's rumoured
they'll be joining the official list soon.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:38.340
By the way, Vanellope taking selfies with
the princesses doesn't appear in the movie

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:42.349
either, though it's unclear if that's part
of a scene cut from the film or a moment just

00:02:42.349 --> 00:02:44.470
created for marketing.

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:48.410
Just before Vanellope and the Disney princesses
meet, there was going to be another extended

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:50.460
Star Wars crossover scene.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:54.569
After the Hoodie Princess gets accused of
peddling unauthorised clickbait at OhMyDisney,

00:02:54.569 --> 00:02:58.849
she escapes from the Stormtroopers and, in
an extended version of this scene, Vanellope

00:02:58.849 --> 00:03:04.069
jumped onto Dumbo and flew off with the little
elephant while getting chased by TIE fighters.

00:03:04.069 --> 00:03:08.270
In the final movie, the Star Wars chase is
stripped right back and shows Vanellope fleeing

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:12.650
on foot from the Stormtroopers before cutting
straight to her glitching into the princess

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:14.489
room backstage.

00:03:14.489 --> 00:03:19.130
Another scene we never saw involved a joke
at the expense of Star Wars baddie Kylo Ren.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:23.739
LucasFilm objected to how he was going to
be portrayed in the animated movie.

00:03:23.739 --> 00:03:27.629
Co-director Rich Moore explained there was
a joke "about Kylo Ren being kind of a spoiled

00:03:27.629 --> 00:03:31.629
child" but after they took it to LucasFilm
to show them what they were doing "they said

00:03:31.629 --> 00:03:34.330
[…] well, we'd prefer that you don't show
him [like that].

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:37.770
You know, he is our villain, and we'd prefer
you don't do that."

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:42.650
It seems a shame this Kylo Ren cameo got cut
as the jokes in Ralph Breaks The Internet

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:47.300
are generally gentle jibes that affectionately
parody characters from Disney's broad range

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:48.569
of properties.

00:03:48.569 --> 00:03:52.900
And I imagine the Kylo Ren joke would've got
quite a few laughs especially as the Star

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:57.660
Wars villain certainly has form when it comes
to acting out like a spoiled child.

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:01.410
It's also possible that, with the current
Star Wars trilogy about to complete in Episode

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:05.319
9, LucasFilm were concerned the joke might
cause some kind of problem for where they're

00:04:05.319 --> 00:04:07.640
taking Kylo Ren in their next movie.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:12.870
A Star Wars-inspired character, Double Dan,
who has a Jabba the Hutt-style appearance,

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:15.260
also had an additional scene deleted.

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:20.449
When Ralph goes to the Darknet with Spamley,
he meets the half-human half-worm character

00:04:20.449 --> 00:04:23.860
[Double Dan] and the second head he has living
in his neck.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:24.860
"Yeuk!"

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:25.960
"What are you doing here?"

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:28.810
"The reason I came to your neck of the face."

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:30.289
"I mean there's a face in your neck!"

00:04:30.289 --> 00:04:32.090
"Ha ha, I mean woods, neck of the woods!"

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:35.749
Originally, there was going to be a "Lady
and the Tramp" moment where we see the two

00:04:35.749 --> 00:04:40.349
Dans eating a virus together, and just like
that iconic spaghetti and meatballs scene,

00:04:40.349 --> 00:04:41.759
the two Dans end up kissing.

00:04:41.759 --> 00:04:47.539
There's a stack of Disney cameos in the movie's
OhMyDisney scenes, but originally the four

00:04:47.539 --> 00:04:52.210
lead characters from the popular 80s sitcom
The Golden Girls were also going to make an

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:53.210
appearance.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:57.169
The idea for these cameos came when the filmmakers
were researching the real-life OhMyDisney

00:04:57.169 --> 00:05:00.520
website and noticed The Golden Girls featured
heavily there.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:04.860
However, during early screenings of Wreck-It
Ralph 2, some people were confused about why

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:09.300
Blanche, Rose, Dorothy and Sophia were in
the scene and so they ended up being cut from

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:10.300
the film.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:15.029
Although the hit sitcom aired on NBC it was
produced by Disney and the four actresses

00:05:15.029 --> 00:05:19.990
received Disney Legends awards in 2009, so
it is a real shame they didn't make it into

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:20.990
the movie.

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:25.009
In fact, co-director Phil Johnston has said
it's one of his biggest regrets.

00:05:25.009 --> 00:05:29.319
Although fan favourite Tinkerbell did make
a very brief appearance in Wreck-It Ralph

00:05:29.319 --> 00:05:33.949
2 when Vanellope rushed past her backstage
at OhMyDisney, originally, Disney's best-known

00:05:33.949 --> 00:05:36.270
fairy had a larger role in the movie.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:40.979
In footage shown at D23, there was a scene
where "Tinker Bell tickles Ralph's nose until

00:05:40.979 --> 00:05:43.719
he insults her by calling her 'Stinker Smell'."

00:05:43.719 --> 00:05:47.569
This might have been a fun little moment,
so I imagine it was cut simply because the

00:05:47.569 --> 00:05:51.779
filmmakers changed the story and Ralph no
longer accompanied Vanellope on her visit

00:05:51.779 --> 00:05:52.779
to OhMyDisney.

00:05:52.779 --> 00:05:57.899
Fans of Fix-It Felix and Calhoun may be a
little disappointed that the pair got a much

00:05:57.899 --> 00:06:02.039
smaller part in the sequel, although they
did get to deliver some hilarious perfect

00:06:02.039 --> 00:06:05.499
parenting advice that none of us will ever
know the truth about!

00:06:05.499 --> 00:06:10.110
But the original story envisioned a much bigger
role for the couple as during the second act

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:13.940
we would have seen how the pair were coping
with trying to bring up a horde of unruly

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:14.940
racers.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:18.349
The way this was initially going to happen
was that there was going to be another character

00:06:18.349 --> 00:06:23.490
in the movie called Bev, who was not only
the head of an antivirus company but was also

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:26.809
a secret villain who was tracking what Ralph
was doing on the internet which led her to

00:06:26.809 --> 00:06:27.809
the arcade.

00:06:27.809 --> 00:06:31.680
By returning to the arcade midway through
the movie, we would have got more screen time

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:37.639
with Felix and Calhoun, but once the Bev anti-virus
plot was dropped, of course, that didn't happen.

00:06:37.639 --> 00:06:42.000
It does feel like the duo's story was a touch
abbreviated with something missing in the

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:45.139
middle, but at least now we know why it feels
like that.

00:06:45.139 --> 00:06:49.719
The Pancake-Milkshake scene was an instant
hit when it debuted in the film's first trailer,

00:06:49.719 --> 00:06:53.719
and originally it was supposed to appear in
the main part of the movie with Ralph and

00:06:53.719 --> 00:06:56.220
Vanellope visiting the game when they were
loot-hunting.

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:57.220
"Woh.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:58.220
Games!"

00:06:58.220 --> 00:06:59.349
"Out of my way kid."

00:06:59.349 --> 00:07:00.349
"Pancake.

00:07:00.349 --> 00:07:01.349
Milkshake."

00:07:01.349 --> 00:07:02.349
"Milkshake.

00:07:02.349 --> 00:07:03.349
Huh.

00:07:03.349 --> 00:07:04.349
I'm starting to understand why people like
this game."

00:07:04.349 --> 00:07:05.349
"Eat, eat!"

00:07:05.349 --> 00:07:08.399
"Err, Ralph you might wanna try feeding the
kitty for a little while."

00:07:08.399 --> 00:07:09.399
"No!

00:07:09.399 --> 00:07:16.479
The kitty gets the milkshake, the bunny gets
the pancake..."

00:07:16.479 --> 00:07:27.059
In fact, this scene was one of the first ideas
to be fully animated.

00:07:27.059 --> 00:07:31.399
However, as the story developed, the directors
felt that Ralph and Vanellope's loot-hunting

00:07:31.399 --> 00:07:36.339
activities were dragging out too long so they
deleted the scene and went straight to Slaughter

00:07:36.339 --> 00:07:39.949
Race instead to move the plot forward more
quickly.

00:07:39.949 --> 00:07:43.779
The problem was that, at that point, Disney
had already started commissioning production

00:07:43.779 --> 00:07:47.449
of Funko Pops, plushes, and other toys for
the bunny and the cat.

00:07:47.449 --> 00:07:52.199
Fortunately, co-writer and director Phil Johnston
came up with the idea of keeping the scene

00:07:52.199 --> 00:07:55.610
as a mid-credits stinger and turning it into
a deliciously meta-joke.

00:07:55.610 --> 00:08:00.339
Funnily enough, Johnston's fellow Wreck-It
Ralph 2 director Rich Moore has confessed

00:08:00.339 --> 00:08:04.349
that he's exactly the kind of person who goes
crazy when a trailer scene doesn't show up

00:08:04.349 --> 00:08:05.990
in the film he's watching.

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:10.279
I wonder if he's also the kind of person who
likes watching deleted scenes videos on YouTube!

00:08:10.279 --> 00:08:14.800
By the way, I reveal how Ralph Breaks The
Internet trolls all us Disney, Marvel and

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:20.090
Pixar fans in my other video, which I'll add
links to at the end, and in the video description.

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:23.949
While developing the first Wreck-It Ralph
movie, Disney managed to secure the rights

00:08:23.949 --> 00:08:27.179
to include Mario and Luigi from the Super
Mario games.

00:08:27.179 --> 00:08:31.069
In the end, though the filmmakers couldn't
find a good way to include the famous video

00:08:31.069 --> 00:08:35.440
game characters in the movie, however, Rich
Moore did state that he wanted Mario to appear

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:36.440
in the sequel.

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:40.650
Sadly, though by the time the sequel entered
development, the rights were no longer available

00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:44.810
to Disney, meaning everyone's favourite Italian
plumber couldn't appear in Ralph Breaks The

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:46.520
Internet.

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:50.400
Marvel Comics legend Stan Lee passed away
shortly before the release of the Wreck-It

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:54.570
Ralph sequel, making his brief appearance
in the film a particularly poignant moment

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:55.570
for Marvel fans.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:09:00.180
And it's especially sad that originally a
much longer extended scene was planned for

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:01.230
the comic-book superstar.

00:09:01.230 --> 00:09:06.500
An earlier version of Lee's cameo featured
a device called the Marvelizer where avatars

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:10.420
for net users would transform into a Marvel
character after walking through a machine

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:12.950
that looked similar to a metal detector.

00:09:12.950 --> 00:09:16.600
Stan Lee would also have walked through the
machine, but unfortunately when the scene

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:21.210
ended up on the cutting room floor we never
got to see which Marvel character Disney thought

00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:23.050
Stan Lee was.

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:27.190
Marvel fans will know there's a theory that
Stan Lee's cameos in the MCU mean he's a character

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:31.710
known as Uatu the Watcher and I wonder whether
we might have seen that theory confirmed.

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:36.290
Now, do you wish any of these deleted scenes
and cameos were in the final film?

